# AbuBank — environment template (placeholders only; never commit a real .env).
# Authoritative policy: docs/abuai/ENV_CONTRACT.md + docs/engineering-os/VERSION_CONTRACT.md
# Enforced by: src/clientProviderKeyContract.test.ts, src/screens/AbuAI/serverProxyContract.test.ts

# ── SERVER-ONLY (billable). Set in Vercel Project → Environment Variables. ──
# Never expose as VITE_*. Used by api/abuai-chat, abuai-online, abuai-stt,
# abuai-tts, realtime-token.
OPENAI_API_KEY=your_openai_api_key_here

# ── CLIENT-ALLOWED (free-tier, rate-limited, non-billable). Baked into the bundle by design. ──
VITE_GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key_here
VITE_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# ── DEV-ONLY. Do NOT set these in the production/build environment. ──
# The Vite dev server proxy (vite.config.ts) may read VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY for a
# local /api/abuai-chat. If set in a *build* env, Vite would bake this BILLABLE
# key into the public JS bundle. The build-time guard
# scripts/check-client-secret-leak.cjs blocks that. Leave unset in prod.
# VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=dev_only_never_in_build
# VITE_AZURE_TTS_KEY=dev_only_never_in_build
